> Conclusion

The controlled fusion check has zero printed value/gradient error and preserves
35 negative outputs. The 2174882-scalar detector makes 384 Adam updates,
selecting the last epoch, 12, at validation AP50 0.254823. On the eight test scenes/23 digits,
100 proposals/image cover 1.000000/0.652174 at IoU 0.5/0.7. Final AP50/AP75/AP50:95
are 0.262407/0.057187/0.108975, with 181 retained class-specific detections.
The bounded fit has limited detection quality, and the galleries visibly retain
many extra boxes. These results demonstrate the pipeline and its limitations;
they do not reproduce the paper's accuracy.

The odd-grid oracle and derivative checks establish the unsmoothed top-down invariant before fitting. Constant-level pooling exposes discrete scale routing and order restoration. The full model then fits all compact source parameters visibly, with original training/test pixels and selected proposal/detection galleries. This bounded run reports its outcomes without claiming paper accuracy, runtime speedups or a cross-architecture ranking.

> References

- [Lin et al. (2017), Feature Pyramid Networks for Object Detection](https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.03144).
- [TorchVision official feature_pyramid_network.py](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/main/torchvision/ops/feature_pyramid_network.py).
- [Ren et al. (2015), Faster R-CNN](https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01497).
